# The callback of the OAuth flow in a backend for frontend (BFF). The browser is the environment of the
# interaction and no lifeline: its call comes in through a gate on the frame, the answer goes back through
# the gate, the audit event leaves to the right. State invariants say what must hold at that point; the
# token exchange carries its transmission time, neg forbids redeeming the code twice.
diagram sequence "OAuth-Callback verarbeiten" subtitle="Gates am Rahmen, Zustandsinvarianten, Nachricht mit Dauer, neg" locale=de
frame "OAuth-Callback"
participant bff "Backend for Frontend" stereotype="service"
participant idp "Autorisierungsserver" external
database sessions "Session-Store"
msg gate -> bff "GET /callback?code&state" id=callback
invariant "state = gespeicherter state" on=bff
msg bff -> idp "POST /oauth/token (code, code_verifier)" duration="≤ 800 ms"
msg idp --> bff "ID-, Access- und Refresh-Token"
msg bff -> bff "ID-Token prüfen (Signatur, iss, aud, nonce)"
msg bff -> sessions "SET session (Tokens verschlüsselt)"
msg sessions --> bff "ok"
invariant "Angemeldet" on=bff state
msg bff --> gate "302 Location: / · Set-Cookie: sid" id=done
msg bff ~> gate "audit: login.erfolgt"
neg
  msg bff -> idp "POST /oauth/token (derselbe code)"
  msg idp --> bff "neue Tokens"
note "Ein Code gilt genau einmal: der zweite Tausch muss scheitern." over=bff,idp
duration callback done "≤ 2 s"
